KG42.register("rules-7502addcfcfa55a3ee9b8627",{"id":"41-data_center_local_markets::v141-c-R003","paper":"41-data_center_local_markets","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The proposed price must lie strictly between the negative and positive grid retail price. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price in each local energy market and time slot under the proposed model. The CSP’s proposed price must be zero. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price for each IDC’s local energy market and time slot. Condition: The IDC’s net-load is zero. The proposed price must have the same sign as the IDC’s net-load. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price for each IDC’s local energy market and time slot. Condition: The IDC’s net-load is nonzero.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price for each IDC’s local energy market and time slot. | The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price in each local energy market and time slot under the proposed model.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E18"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-price","symbol":"\\pi_k^T(t)","meaning":"Energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot; positive values denote purchase price and negative values denote selling price.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued continuous signed price; positive = purchase price, negative = selling price","unit":"$/kWh","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E18"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R003-x-net-load","symbol":"P_k^N(t)","meaning":"Net-load of the kth IDC at the tth time slot; positive means the IDC needs to buy energy from external sources and negative means it has surplus energy to sell.","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued net load (kW); sign gives buy/sell direction","unit":"kW","indices":["k","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E18"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-retail-price","symbol":"\\pi_k^{RET}","meaning":"Electricity retail price in the kth region, used as the bound on the CSP's proposed local-market price.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"$ (as printed; Eq. (26) compares it with the $/kWh price)","indices":["k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E18"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The proposed price must lie strictly between the negative and positive grid retail price. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price in each local energy market and time slot under the proposed model.","expression":"-\\pi_k^{RET}\u003c\\pi_k^T(t)\u003c\\pi_k^{RET},\\quad \\forall k,t","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-price"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-theta-retail-price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E09","v141-b-g01-E18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The CSP’s proposed price must be zero. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price for each IDC’s local energy market and time slot. Condition: The IDC’s net-load is zero.","expression":"\\forall k,t:\\; P_k^N(t)=0 \\Rightarrow \\pi_k^T(t)=0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R003-x-net-load"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The proposed price must have the same sign as the IDC’s net-load. Scope: The CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price for each IDC’s local energy market and time slot. Condition: The IDC’s net-load is nonzero.","expression":"\\forall k,t:\\; P_k^N(t)\\ne0 \\Rightarrow \\pi_k^T(t)\\cdot P_k^N(t)>0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R003-x-price","v141-c-R003-x-net-load"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E18"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.3 Price-demand elasticity model","anchor_text":"estimated as: 3. εk(t)ET0k (t)ETk (t) = πTk (t) + (1 −εk(t))ET0k (t) (7) πT0k (t) PNk Without loss o","equation_id":"Eq. (7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In each time slot, the CSP proposes energy purchase/selling prices to other participants in the local energy markets, either through auction-based mechanisms or P2P negotiations. Under an energy purchase/selling price, the amount of energy that the CSP can purchase from/sell to the market can be estimated through a price-demand elasticity model (Eq. (6)), which describes the relationship between the price signal and the demand. \\epsilon_k(t)=\\frac{(E_k^T(t)-E_k^{T0}(t))/E_k^{T0}(t)}{(\\pi_k^T(t)-\\pi_k^{T0}(t))/\\pi_k^{T0}(t)},\\quad E_k^{T0}(t)\\ne0 \\tag{6} E_k^T(t)=\\frac{\\epsilon_k(t)E_k^{T0}(t)}{\\pi_k^{T0}(t)}\\pi_k^T(t)+(1-\\epsilon_k(t))E_k^{T0}(t) \\tag{7} Obviously, ε_k(t) is positive when the CSP purchases energy, and is negative when it sells energy in the kth local energy market. Without loss of generality, we use positive and negative values of π_k^T(t) to indicate the energy purchase and selling price proposed by the CSP in the local energy market, respectively. The energy purchase/selling demand E_k^T(t) is a non-negative value."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2.2 / 3.2.3 BESS and energy trading constraints","anchor_text":"Electric Power Systems Research 205 (2022) 107760 e­ ⎛ ⎧ ( ( ) ( ) t ≥0 t −1)+PCH/DISk t ⋅ηCH⋅ΔT PCH","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"-\\pi_k^{RET}\u003c\\pi_k^T(t)\u003c\\pi_k^{RET},\\forall k,t \\tag{26} \\begin{cases}\\pi_k^T(t)=0 & P_k^N(t)=0,\\forall k,t\\\\\\pi_k^T(t)\\cdot P_k^N(t)>0 & P_k^N(t)\\ne0,\\forall k,t\\end{cases} \\tag{27} -P_k^L\\le P_k^N(t)\\le P_k^L,\\forall k,t \\tag{28} Constraint (26) ensures that the energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP does not excess the grid retail price. Constraint (27) describes the relationship between each IDC’s net-load and the proposed energy purchase/selling price: if the net-load is zero, the CSP’s proposed price should also be zero. Otherwise, the proposed price should be with the same sign as the net-load, indicating the CSP should either purchase from or sell energy to the markets. Constraint (28) ensures that each IDC’s net-load flow should be constrained by the capacity limit of its connected power line."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p02-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"Nomenclature","anchor_text":"PpVariables PiAk(t) Number of requests arriving at the kth IDC in the tth time PU slot εkBk(t) Numbe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"πTk(t) Energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($/kWh); ETk(t) Estimated energy purchase/selling volume under πTk(t)(kWh); CDEMk(t) Cost/revenue in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($); PNk(t) Net-load of the kth IDC at the tth time slot (kW); εk(t) Price-demand elasticity factor of the kth IDC in the tth time slot; πT0k(t) Reference energy purchase/selling price in the kth local energy market in the tth time slot ($); ET0k(t) Reference energy demand under πT0k(t)(kWh); πRETk Electricity retail price at the kth region ($); PLk Capacity of the power line connecting the kth IDC and the grid (kW)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E13","location":{"location_id":"src-307a684414-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.1.3 Energy trading cost/revenue from the local energy markets","anchor_text":"3.1.3. Energy trading cost/revenue from the local energy markets For each IDC, its net-load at the t","equation_id":"Eq. (14)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_k^N(t)=P_k^{IDC}(t)+P_k^{CH/DIS}(t)-P_k^{RES}(t) \\tag{12} P_k^{RES}(t)=\\beta_k^{RES}(t)\\cdot P_k^{RES} \\tag{13} C_k^{DEM}(t)=\\pi_k^T(t)\\cdot\\min\\left\\{\\left|P_k^N(t)\\cdot\\Delta T\\right|,E_k^T(t)\\right\\} \\tag{14} A positive value of P_k^N(t) indicates that the IDC needs to buy energy from external sources (i.e. the local energy market and/or the grid), while a negative value indicates that the IDC has surplus energy to sell to other customers. On the basis of the CSP’s proposed energy purchase/selling price in the kth local energy market, the corresponding amount of energy that the CSP can buy from/sell to the market can be estimated following Eq. (7). Then, the cost/revenue of the CSP from the kth local energy market is calculated as Eq. (14)."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","quote":"-\\pi_k^{RET}\u003c\\pi_k^T(t)\u003c\\pi_k^{RET},\\forall k,t \\tag{26}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","quote":"Constraint (26) ensures that the energy purchase/selling price proposed by the CSP does not excess the grid retail price."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E09","quote":"In each time slot, the CSP proposes energy purchase/selling prices to other participants in the local energy markets, either through auction-based mechanisms or P2P negotiations."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","quote":"if the net-load is zero, the CSP’s proposed price should also be zero."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E18","quote":"Otherwise, the proposed price should be with the same sign as the net-load, indicating the CSP should either purchase from or sell energy to the markets."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"07482b6c2c13f569c1de8b5a537330c925b1b353fbb41431a82d443ee8ff7430","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source explicitly gives the price-bound and sign constraints in Eqs. (26)-(27) of v141-b-g01-E18 and defines the referenced price, net-load, and retail-price symbols in v141-b-g01-E03. The three C.1 branches are transcribed as the strict retail-price bound, the zero-price branch, and the nonzero net-load sign branch. B evidence remains unreviewed; this formalization does not assert independent source audit.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-price","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The CSP's proposed energy purchase/selling price is the operand of the approved price-signal coordination function."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-x-net-load","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The frozen graph has no separate net-load node; P_k^N(t) is the conditioning operational quantity that selects the zero-price or same-sign branch in Eq. (27), so it attaches to the approved price-signal function."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-theta-retail-price","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The regional retail price is the fixed bound appearing in the strict price-signal inequality in Eq. (26)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Eq. (26) is the strict bound on the CSP's proposed price signal and binds directly to the sole approved function node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The zero-price branch of Eq. (27) is a conditional condition on the price signal when the IDC net-load is zero."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The nonzero net-load branch of Eq. (27) is the same-sign condition linking the price signal to net-load."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
